# What may reach the Docker daemon.
#
# Deny-by-default: everything is excluded, then the few paths the build
# genuinely needs are added back. An allow-list is the only version of this
# file that stays correct -- a deny-list silently starts shipping every new
# file someone adds to the repo, and the first time that matters is the first
# time it ships a credential.
*

# --- what the build actually needs ------------------------------------------
# The package source and its metadata, to build a wheel.
!src/
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE

# The resolved, hashed dependency set. Without this the image would be built
# from version ranges and two builds a week apart could differ.
!requirements-api.txt

# The persisted vector index. Not needed by demo/stub traffic, which is pure
# BM25, but hybrid retrieval cannot be demonstrated without it. Copied to an
# explicit path and pointed at by KB_VECTOR_INDEX_PATH; see the Dockerfile.
!data/kb_vectors.db

# --- re-excluded, even under the paths added back above ---------------------
# `*` above does not reach inside an un-ignored directory, so src/ needs its
# own exclusions.
src/**/__pycache__/
src/**/*.pyc
src/**/*.pyo

# --- never, under any circumstance ------------------------------------------
# These are already covered by `*`. They are named anyway: this file is read by
# people deciding whether a secret can reach the daemon, and "it is implied by
# a wildcard three screens up" is not the answer that question deserves.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
.git/
.gitignore
secrets/
**/secrets/
.streamlit/
